AB  - Fashion-centered e-commerce is yet to overcome the challenge of accurate visualization of clothing and accessories online; we are addressing this issue in this paper with a real-time, browser-based Augmented Reality (AR) virtual tryon (VTO) application developed on React and three.js. The system uses the MediaPipe Holistic model through the JavaScript API to extract both detailed facial landmarks (478 points) and body pose landmarks (33 points) from a standard webcam stream. With that information, customers will be able to test a variety of 3D products - glasses, earrings, necklaces and T-shirts - right within a single integrated web page. We portray virtual objects in three.js and attach them to the body by calculating the landmarks smoothly and scaling and rotating them, ensuring smooth real-time alignment. This paper presents a dynamic face occlusion mesh and a single multi-accessory alignment pipeline, which makes it possible to render realistically in the browser. The proposed system can offer real-time performance without any specialized hardware, which means that it can be scaled in place of applications in ecommerce. The system also includes an AI-based recommendation module, which is generative and offers real-time suggestions of accessories, based on the user's visual context and selected accessories.
